# Routed S3 refusal — read-only decision brief, 2026-08-27

## Root decision requested

Approve a narrowly scoped **fixture/profile migration only**, not a production fix or failure waiver. The exact routed S3 expectation is obsolete under the already explicit snapshot-marker contract. No repository edit, assertion/result change, staging or commit was made. No superiority, full-green or whole-product acceptance claim is supported.

Proposed write scope, ONLY after root approval: `tests/stress/adapters/remote-safe-workflows.test.ts:17,45-69` and a root-designated new migration evidence/report path. Give the fixture an explicit expected removal profile (S3 snapshot-marker; stock WebDAV unsupported), verify the advertised capability rather than infer it from the backend name, and split the final assertions accordingly. Proposed S3 title: `s3: named-file cleanup leaves parents and snapshot rmdir deletes only the empty marker`; retain the WebDAV refusal title. Do not accept either outcome opportunistically or simply drop the rejection assertion. Preserve the original fixture/result bytes in the original frozen cohort and record the migration separately.

- Retain shared exact named-file cleanup, binary payload and sentinel assertions.
- S3: require `snapshotRmdir === true`; `rmdir(nested)` fulfills; exactly one mutation deletes `{Bucket: "safe-workflows", Key: "work/scratch/nested/"}`. Compare the complete object snapshot against the old snapshot minus only this marker; `/work` and `/work/scratch` remain, sentinel bytes remain `[255,3]`, and this quiescent fixture's `nested` path becomes ENOENT.
- WebDAV: retain the exact FsError ENOTSUP/syscall `rmdir`/requested-path rejection, zero mutations, unchanged snapshot and all three directories. No stock WebDAV capability promotion or recursive DELETE exception.
- Required accompanying positive/negative controls: observed file/nested-file/nested-marker descendants => ENOTEMPTY/no deletion; post-LIST byte child AND nested marker/bytes survive successful exact-marker deletion, potentially leaving the directory visible; complete pagination before DELETE; incomplete LIST/vanished marker/ambiguous or implicit representation refuse; pre-abort/root/readonly protection; conditional-operation capabilities remain false when unverified; unknown authority remains ENOTSUP/no publication. Existing selected controls below supply bounded evidence, not universal guarantees.

