Both: process status **1**, tests 1/pass 0/fail 1/skip 0, the same `Missing expected rejection.` and original `58:5` assertion. No shell command is under test: the exact operation is VFS `rmdir("/work/scratch/nested")` with options omitted, fulfilling with undefined, not a shell exit status.

Input: `MockS3Client({buckets:["safe-workflows"]})`, `S3FileSystem({transport:mock,bucket:"safe-workflows"})`, no prefix or special removal options. `mkdir("/work/scratch/nested", {recursive:true})`; write `owned-file` with helper `binary` (4099 bytes, byte i = i % 256; SHA256 `60a62725a6589b4c56d914f383935cf1f09fdb4c6e6814c1545d5ade78281416`); write `/sentinel` bytes `[255,3]`; `rm(nested + "/owned-file")`. Immediately before rmdir, object keys are `work/`, `work/scratch/`, `work/scratch/nested/` (zero bytes each), `sentinel` (2 bytes). No children remain. Instrumented replay confirms precisely the marker deletion above, two parent markers unchanged, sentinel unchanged, nested stat ENOENT.

WebDAV uses `new MockDav()` and `WebDavFileSystem({baseUrl:"https://example.test/dav/",fetch:mock.fetch})`, same input calls. It rejects with `FsError`, ENOTSUP, syscall rmdir, requested nested path, message `ENOTSUP: rmdir has no safe portable WebDAV equivalent, rmdir '/work/scratch/nested'`; operation requests are PROPFIND only, all entries/bytes unchanged. These are stock-adapter mocked controls, NOT a fresh deployed-service acceptance claim.

